Reading: the nominal valley chain lands ABOVE the 6 EUR gate, and
the conventional independence analysis prices the gate at one
number — a number that is pure assumption: the distribution-free
p-box spans the full [0, 100], undetermined. The one-at-a-time
table names the flippers: the waste-heat contract and the
dispensing tariff EACH carry the gate at their favourable ends;
utilization — the valley's design pride — cannot do it alone.
Sobol agrees and ranks the rest: the electrolyser specs that
dominate the literature are minority shareholders of the variance.
For TRIERES: price the heat contract and the dispensing business
model FIRST; CF is a multiplier, not a saviour. The shares are a
map drawn under the assumption the p-box refuses — the interval
is the deliverable, the map is how you shrink it.
